From: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lib: umash: add umash_params_init_random() helper

The nft_set_hash.c UMASH call site (999-umash-03) hand-rolls a
get_random_bytes()+umash_params_prepare() retry loop for its
DO_ONCE-guarded lazy init. The next three call sites (inet/inet6
established-hash, UDP portaddr hash) all want the exact same thing,
so pull it into a header-only inline helper instead of copy-pasting
the loop a fourth time.

DO_ONCE() itself still lives at each call site (it needs its own
static key + "done" flag per site), this just removes the boilerplate
of what runs the first time.

Signed-off-by: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
---
--- a/include/linux/umash.h
+++ b/include/linux/umash.h
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 #define _LINUX_UMASH_H

 #include <linux/types.h>
+#include <linux/random.h>

 enum { UMASH_OH_PARAM_COUNT = 32, UMASH_OH_TWISTING_COUNT = 2 };

@@ -66,4 +67,22 @@ bool umash_params_prepare(struct umash_params *params);
  */
 u64 umash_full(const struct umash_params *params, u64 seed, const void *data, size_t n_bytes);

+/*
+ * Convenience helper for call sites that just want a randomly-keyed
+ * umash_params with no special handling: retries until
+ * umash_params_prepare() accepts the random bytes (astronomically
+ * unlikely to loop more than once). Pair with DO_ONCE() at each call
+ * site for lazy, thread/interrupt-safe, exactly-once init:
+ *
+ *   static struct umash_params __read_mostly my_params;
+ *   ...
+ *   DO_ONCE(umash_params_init_random, &my_params);
+ */
+static inline void umash_params_init_random(struct umash_params *params)
+{
+	do {
+		get_random_bytes(params, sizeof(*params));
+	} while (!umash_params_prepare(params));
+}
+
 #endif /* _LINUX_UMASH_H */
